        "text": "I thoroughly enjoyed my time here and despite not being an 'attractive' temple it's very spiritual and a very important religious place for Hindus. \nI recommend visiting around 5 so you have some time to look around before the music begins at 6 in the evening - this happens every day and really made the experience for me. It was quite odd yet moving to experience a cremation on one side of the river with singing, dancing and a celebratory feel on the other side as the crowd sang songs worshipping shiva. \nAn incredible unique place well worth the high entrance fee",
