        "title": "Only for Hindu",
        "text": "I've visited this temple compound during my one day guided tour around 4 major tourist attractions in Kathmandu, all in UNESCO Heritage sites list. Temple itself is open only for Hindu believers, so I couldn't enter, but I heard guide explanation about the facade, and history of the temple and its importance in Hindu religion. Temple is on the bank of Bagmati river which itself is considered by Hindus and Buddhists as a holy river as continues to Ganges, and purifies the people spiritually. That's why many Hindus are cremated on the banks of this holy river, near the temple.",
