        "title": "Worthwhile - but at a cost!",
        "text": "We were a little shaken to be taken 1000 RS out of our pockets for a visit here. this is- even for westerners- something we hardly ever pay for Sightseeing, keeping in mind that we were not even allowed (as non-Hindus) to go into the main temple.\nAt Durbar Square It is different because it is obvious you make a contribution to the rebuilding after the earthquake (it^s also 1000 RS there) \n\na Little disturbing or funny is also, that the \"Sadhus\" almost get a little angry if offered \"only\" 50 Rs for a Foto (they just sit there and smoke all day... well... it^s your choice I guess but I don^t quite approve...)\n\nNonetheless, if you take your time to stroll around and take in the atmosphere, you feel that despite the commerce this place is special- especially with the cremations going on of course... bear in mind to pay respect and dont shove your camera lens into the ongoing cremation- stay away.",
